 },
 "scope_notes": "Much of the diff is mechanical boilerplate removal of ECC_Context across binaries, tests, and benchmarks, as well as scripted-diff replacements of secp256k1_context_static.",
 "changed_since_previous": "Rather than moving ECC_Context management into separate ecc_context and ecc_init files, ECC_Context is completely eliminated; both signing and public contexts are now created lazily on first use.",
 "card": "Plugs Bitcoin Core's hardware-optimized SHA256 compression routine into libsecp256k1 contexts and removes the ECC_Context RAII class across the codebase in favor of lazily initialized global contexts. Replaces secp256k1_context_static across pubkey, MuSig2, and BIP352 operations so they can leverage hardware acceleration. Benchmarks on ARM64 show a 13% speedup for ECDSA signing and a 7% speedup for Schnorr signing, with minimal impact on signature verification. No dependencies are listed.",
